Z||000011||cadero2dmax||10-31-2001||11:06 PM||||Joe<P>Would you be willing to help me with graphics on the Grassroots Motorsports $2002 Challenge Fiero with your new viny cutter?<P>In case you are not aware of this project, the Challenge is a 3 tiered competition. It consists of a drag race, an autocross, and judging. The catch is, you can't spend more than $2002 on the car, including the purchase price. <P>I am building a 4.9 powered 86 coupe with a TH125 in an '88 cradle. I can make a Fiero handle, and with this powertrain, should be able to finish pretty high in points in both the drags and autocross. But the judging is something I am worried about.<P>What graphics I have in mind should be pretty simple and straight forward, all lettering, but the locals all want more than the $2002 budget would allow (I won't have a lot left after I get the car competitive).<P>Would you be interested, or able to help for cost of material + a fair price for your talents?<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000012||tgowens||10-31-2001||11:24 PM||||There were stripe kits made by Pontiac for the Fiero --<P>1984 P Stripes/Body (Y82)<BR>1984-1987 P Stripes/Body Spoiler & Molding<P>They were part # 10032863 Front end panel right and #10032864 Front end panel left. #10032869 Fender right and #10032870 Fender left. #10032871 Door. #10032872 Rear quarter panel right and #10032873 Rear quarter panel left.10032866 rear fascia left and #10032865 rear fascia right.<P>These were primarily for the Indy option (Y82)<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
