Z||000028||cadero2dmax||11-05-2001||08:59 AM||||Well, I thought I had a commercial     source for my graphics. But the owner of the shop wanted a huge (by comparison) logo put on the car. I was willing to put his logo in 4" lettering(you know, "Graphics by - - - - ") on the back window or vertical part of the trunk, but that wasn't good enough.<P>This guy wanted a NASCAR sponsership sized logo in exchange for a $40 or so price cut. (He can write the entire thing off as advertisement).<P>As I stated earlier, this car will probably be in a National magazine, possibly even a feature or (if it looks and does well enough) on the cover. <P>It will also be in shows and competitions after we get done with the Challenge. I will start by having it at Ed's Swap Meet in April. It will be autocrossed in SM2, at the drags for fun, and on the road racing course in various SCCA and NASA touring events. <P>That is a lot of exposure for a $40 price cut on an approximate $80 job, especially when the logo was as big or bigger than the graphics he was to make.<P>I did volunteer to do his "plan" if he wanted to do a FULL sponsorship. :-)<P>Needless to say, I declined this offer. Joe volunteered to cut some letters for me when he gets his vinyl cutter, so we will exercise some patience.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>84 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||7
