Z||000045||Joe Torma||11-09-2001||02:40 PM||||Hmmm...interesting, JP.  Looks good!  I'm going to have to figure out the license place area.  Was it "pieced"?<P>I should have everything ready early next week.  I'm quitting 1 job, setting up a dedicated computer for cutting and other output, as well as building a special table to make things easy.<P>I haven't forgotten anything I've promised guys!  Just be patient, I hate doing things half-a$$ed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000046||fierojp||11-09-2001||02:47 PM||||Joe,<BR>The stripes I used conformed very well to all body curvature except around the rear license plate area.  I did have to cut out a few fitted pieces for the inside of the license plate cutout.  As you probably noticed, I put the stripes right on the sunroof too.  I thought it came out really nice.  Take your time measuring when you put them on (I put a strip of 2.5 inch masking tape down the center of the car - worked very well - just butted the stripes up against it).  If the stripes are off by a few millimeters, it would be noticeable on parallel stripes!<P>JP||||reg||1
